  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Let V be a variety of groups and let k be an infinite cardinal number. A group\nG ∈ V of rank k is called almost free in V if each of its subgroups of rank less than k\nis contained in a subgroup of G which is free in V. For what k do there exist almost\nfree but not free in B groups of rank k?                                 S. V. Rychkov",
